<title>USA: FSA qualifies 17 issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies 17 issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said it has qualified for bond insurance the following 17 municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Dade County, S.D., Fla. $140 million general obligation school bonds.</p>
<p>--Iowa Great Lakes San., Iowa, $5 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Jefferson, Iowa, $1.3 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Dennis, Mass., $4.44 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Columbia Heights, Minn., $33.5 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Lake of Woods, Minn., $2.940 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Cleveland County, N.C., $6.075 million refunding GOs.</p>
<p>--Madison Boro Board of Education, N.J., $#.982 million school bonds</p>
<p>--Yorkshire CSD, N.Y., $12.250 school district GOs.</p>
<p>--Elmira Heights CSD, N.Y., $4.150 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Niagra Falls, N.Y., $9.5 million school district GOs.</p>
<p>--Warwick, R.I., $9 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Boerne, Texas, $1.730 million tax and rev. certificates.</p>
<p>--La Crosse, Wis., $5.305 million GO prom.</p>
<p>--Elmira Heights CSD, N.Y., $4.15 million school district GOs.</p>
<p>--Rockland, Mass., $4.345 million.</p>
<p>--Oak Lawn, Ill., $5.950 million.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
